cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Choreographic Types"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-13"
abstract: "Pre-registration and research notebook for a graded multiparty-session type theory combining echo loss-grades and epistemic warrants on partial causal orders. The central artefact is K-CUT: the conjecture that grading and transport commute with endpoint projection across a consistent frontier (antichain), splitting into equality on loss-grades/bound on warrants. Agda is the prover: the finite, binary-choice, plain-merge, synchronous fragment is checked under a pinned --safe --without-K gate, with siblings imported at pinned commits; what is and is not proved is ledgered in PROOF-STATUS.adoc. Beyond that fragment (recursion, full merge, asynchrony, data-dependent warrants) K-CUT remains a pre-registration."
authors:
  - family-names: "Jewell"
    given-names: "Jonathan D.A."
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3078-6652"
repository-code: "https://github.com/hyperpolymath/choreographic-types"
